sentence:
Patient data:
Dear dermatologist,

Patient ID: PAT_467;
Image ID: PAT_467_904_235.png;
Diagnosis: BCC (Bacterial Cystic Dermatitis);
Age: 46 years old;
Gender: Female;
Fitzpatrick skin type: 2.0;
Lesion location: back;
Lesion size: 10.0×5.0 mm;
Symptoms: Itching, growth, elevation;
Environmental factors: Piped water exposure, pesticide exposure;
Family history: Father has Pomera; Mother also has Pomera.

Thank you for your assistance.

Best regards,
[Your Name]
Skin lesion description:
The lesion appears roughly oval in shape, though somewhat irregular, and doesn't present with obvious symmetry. Its borders are indistinct and blend into the surrounding skin, without a well-defined edge. The primary color is a pale pink, with areas of deeper reddish-pink at the center and some areas of white/pale discoloration. The lesion is approximately 8-10 millimeters in diameter. The surface texture appears somewhat raised and slightly bumpy, possibly with a subtle crusted or scaling component. There is a mild halo of redness visible around the periphery of the lesion, and the immediate surrounding skin doesn't exhibit significant scaling or other noticeable changes.

Patient data:
Patient details:

