Fitzpatrick Skin Type: 4.0;
Lesion Location: thigh;
Lesion Size: 90.0×20.0 mm;
Symptoms: Itching, growth, pain, changes in lesion, bleeding;
Environmental Factors: Piped water, sewage system;
Family History: Father - Italy; Mother - Italy;
Skin lesion description:
The lesion appears roughly circular, though somewhat irregular in shape, with a noticeable central area of darker, textured material. Its borders are not sharply defined, blending into the surrounding skin. The main color is a mottled mix of grey, brown, and possibly a hint of purple, with a reddish hue visible underneath. It appears to be approximately 6-8 millimeters in diameter. The surface is notably raised and uneven, displaying a bumpy, crusted texture. There’s a subtle area of redness immediately around the base of the lesion and a few small, pale yellow, scale-like spots nearby. The surrounding skin appears generally consistent in color and texture.

Patient data:
Patient details:
- ID: PAT_971; 
- img_id: PAT_971_1847_99.png;
- diagnostic: ACK;
- Age: 64 years old;
- Gender: Female;
- Fitzpatrick skin type: 2.0;
- Lesion location: hand;
- Lesion size: 14.0×13.0 mm;
- Symptoms: Itching;
- Environmental factors: piped water, sewage system, pesticide exposure;
- Family history: father: POMERANIA; mother: POMERANIA
Skin lesion description:
The lesion presents as an approximately 1.5 cm, roughly circular area with a slightly irregular shape. It features a central core of pale yellow, flaky material, which transitions outwards into a ring of raised, reddish-pink skin. The border between the central core and the surrounding pink area isn't sharply defined, appearing somewhat blurred and slightly elevated. A subtle halo of erythema extends outwards from the pink ring onto the surrounding skin, which appears generally normal in color but exhibits some minor textural variation. There is mild scaling noticeable around the periphery of the lesion and a slight glistening quality to the central, flaky area.

