Lesion Size: 10.0×7.0 mm;  
Symptoms: itching, growth, changes in lesion, elevation;  
Environmental Factors: piped water, sewage system;  
Family History: father: Germany, mother: Germany; family cancer history
Skin lesion description:
The lesion presents as an approximately 7mm circular area with a slightly raised, irregular shape. Its border is not well-defined, appearing somewhat blurred where it transitions into the surrounding skin. The primary color is a vibrant pink to red, with a noticeable central area that appears paler and slightly yellowish, and is covered by a small, translucent, scab-like material. The surface has a somewhat uneven texture with a slightly crusted or flaky appearance. A subtle halo of redness extends a few millimeters around the lesion, and the adjacent skin appears generally normal without any significant scaling or other visible changes.

Patient data:
Please note the following details:

Patient ID: PAT_247;
Image ID: PAT_247_1294_292.png;
Diagnosis: BCC (Cleaved Cell);
Age: 58 years;
Gender: Male;
Fitzpatrick Skin Type: 3.0;
Lesion Location: Nose;
Lesion Size: 12.0 x 6.0 mm;
Symptoms: Growth, Changes in lesion, Elevation;
Environmental Factors: Pesticide exposure;
Family History:
- Father: Germany
- Mother: Germany
Skin lesion description:
The lesion appears roughly oval, though somewhat irregular in shape, and is outlined by a purple marker. Its central color is a pale pink, with a slightly darker, reddish hue visible within its core. The lesion appears to be approximately 1.5-2 centimeters in length. The surface texture appears slightly raised and somewhat granular or bumpy. Surrounding the lesion, there is noticeable redness (erythema) extending outwards, and there appears to be some fine scaling of the skin in the immediately adjacent area. The lesion is located on a skin area with visible hair follicles.
